  "problem": "Orlando bought $6$ packages of powdered fertilizer, for which he paid $$96.44.$ Estimate the price of each package by rounding the amount of money he spent to the nearest dollar.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The approximate price of each package is $\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate the price of each package, we need to find an approximation to $96.44÷6.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n96.44\\to 96\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $96$ by $6$ as usual:\n\n$$\n96÷6=16\n$$\n\nTherefore, the approximate price of each package is $$16.$",
